{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1481626-the-fear-of-thin-bloods-is-legit","id":1481626,"title":"The fear of thin-bloods is legit","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-05-21T16:35:27-07:00","id":1481626,"title":"The fear of thin-bloods is legit","content":"Thin-bloods have reason to envy and hate full-blooded vampires. Moreover, they are human enough that many can attack during the day. They are therefore, effectively, a masquerade breech: mostly human creatures who can attack during the day and know vampire secrets.<br /> <br /> Every one of them should, at a minimum, be blood-bound to a full-blooded vampire. Any that display the slightest resistance to blood-bonding should be exterminated.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-21T17:47:51-07:00","id":1481632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1481626-the-fear-of-thin-bloods-is-legit#post1481626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Every one of them should, at a minimum, be blood-bound to a full-blooded vampire. Any that display the slightest resistance to blood-bonding should be exterminated.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the reason they have to hate full-blooded vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-21T18:15:27-07:00","id":1481634,"title":"","content":"It's a vicious circle! Almost as if vampirism were some kind of curse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-21T19:48:08-07:00","id":1481637,"title":"","content":"I can see most vampires seeing this very easily. Especially Camarilla ones, and Noddists (if they aren't fond of Gehenna that is). <br /> <br /> And the worst of it, is that Thinbloods are really off-rules, breaking way too many absolutes from vampirism. Those rule-bending natures can make any game-player in the vampire politics worried.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-21T20:18:05-07:00","id":1481639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Banu_Saulot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1481626-the-fear-of-thin-bloods-is-legit?p=1481637#post1481637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can see most vampires seeing this very easily. Especially Camarilla ones, and Noddists (if they aren't fond of Gehenna that is).<br /> <br /> And the worst of it, is that Thinbloods are really off-rules, breaking way too many absolutes from vampirism. Those rule-bending natures can make any game-player in the vampire politics worried.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, yes, the obsession with controlling all possible factors and unpredictables, no matter how untenable such a prospect might turn into, not to mention sowing the seeds of antagonism, rebellion &amp; resistance in the first place, in the long run.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-22T01:51:34-07:00","id":1481646,"title":"","content":"<b>Tzimisce Me:</b> I agree. The undesirables should only exist for my pleasu...oh Caine I'm becoming my sire.<br /> <br /> <b>Gangel Me:</b> Won't that just make more thin-bloods attack more often? You know, creating an infinite cycle of pain.<br /> <br /> <b>Hecata Me:</b> I agree 100%. <b>Turns around to the thin-bloods</b> Here's a gun, and the address of the prince. Go nuts. This investment better pay off...<b>Plans to bind the ones that become wraiths</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-22T02:17:12-07:00","id":1481647,"title":"","content":"Some vampires truly believe their condition is a &quot;curse&quot; but most probably see it more as a blessing that gives them all sorts of advantages. Thinbloods have weaker powers, so the expectation (whether stated or not) from many vampires is that Thinbloods <i>want</i> to increase their Generation. They're envious and they want to get the full set of vampiric powers. They're going to try and diablarize their way into being a full Kindred. It's a matter of when, not if. Many vampires are going to assume the worst (which isn't necessarily a bad idea when dealing with other monsters).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-22T02:29:33-07:00","id":1481648,"title":"","content":"A scourge was almost always part of my cam chronicles for exactly that reason (+gehenna is here, the end is nigh, let us fight the symptoms). You also can get great antagonists that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This is me, just forgot my PW and changed my email<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8249-crytash\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8249-crytash</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25163-crytash2","name":"Crytash2","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25163_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-22T06:49:55-07:00","id":1481658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crytash2</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1481626-the-fear-of-thin-bloods-is-legit?p=1481648#post1481648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A scourge was almost always part of my cam chronicles for exactly that reason (+gehenna is here, the end is nigh, let us fight the symptoms). You also can get great antagonists that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that gets to the heart of how and why Scourges are useful characters. I don't know that it's ever stated so plainly in text, but they're the muscle of some of the most profoundly paranoid, insecure, and ruthless creatures walking on two legs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-22T16:53:42-07:00","id":1481697,"title":"","content":"i'm currently running a game where all the players are thin blooded (other than a single caitiff) and there hasn't been any moment of envy but, rather, a sense of liberation from the shackles of vampire society and none of them have any desire to diablerise their way up generations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>they/them.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27123-littlewitchmaus","name":"littlewitchmaus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27123_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-23T07:55:21-07:00","id":1481756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1481626-the-fear-of-thin-bloods-is-legit#post1481626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Moreover, they are human enough that many can attack during the day. They are therefore, effectively, a masquerade breech: mostly human creatures who can attack during the day and know vampire secrets.</div> </div> </div> </div>How is this fundamentally different from ghouls?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27061-random-goblin","name":"Random Goblin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27061_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-23T08:12:40-07:00","id":1481759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1481626-the-fear-of-thin-bloods-is-legit?p=1481639#post1481639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, yes, the obsession with controlling all possible factors and unpredictables, no matter how untenable such a prospect might turn into, not to mention sowing the seeds of antagonism, rebellion &amp; resistance in the first place, in the long run.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like our current world political and business practices.<br /> <br /> *Sigh* The most corrupt and out of touch vampires being in power do to having unfair advantages despite lack of qualifications was probably the intended metaphor even in the 90's. I <i>definitely</i> didn't really get that until later in life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-23T08:26:24-07:00","id":1481760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>littlewitchmaus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1481626-the-fear-of-thin-bloods-is-legit?p=1481697#post1481697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">i'm currently running a game where all the players are thin blooded (other than a single caitiff) and there hasn't been any moment of envy but, rather, a sense of liberation from the shackles of vampire society and none of them have any desire to diablerise their way up generations.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds like an awesome campaign.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-24T14:54:01-07:00","id":1481864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1481626-the-fear-of-thin-bloods-is-legit#post1481626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thin-bloods have reason to envy and hate full-blooded vampires. Moreover, they are human enough that many can attack during the day. They are therefore, effectively, a masquerade breech: mostly human creatures who can attack during the day and know vampire secrets.<br /> <br /> Every one of them should, at a minimum, be blood-bound to a full-blooded vampire. Any that display the slightest resistance to blood-bonding should be exterminated.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not to mention they are seen as signs of Gehenna and you know how paranoid elders and ancients are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-28T15:41:04-07:00","id":1482201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1481626-the-fear-of-thin-bloods-is-legit?p=1481760#post1481760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That sounds like an awesome campaign.</div> </div> </div> </div>it has been, so far!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>they/them.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27123-littlewitchmaus","name":"littlewitchmaus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27123_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-31T19:41:40-07:00","id":1482565,"title":"","content":"The best part of Thin Bloods being a threat is that its an entirely self-inflicted one by other vampires, as ToTB and the Week of Nightmares demonstrated. As Reasor said, its almost as if vampirism is a curse, and it always seems to find new and inventive ways to kick the undead in the backside with that fact.<br /> <br /> That said, Thin Bloods being a danger (in a military sense) would require effective leadership and organization to achieve, and that seems to be something they're not really geared to aim for (any more than Anarchs are.) <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25533-mister_dunpeal","name":"Mister_Dunpeal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-01T12:25:31-07:00","id":1482635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mister_Dunpeal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1481626-the-fear-of-thin-bloods-is-legit?p=1482565#post1482565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, Thin Bloods being a danger (in a military sense) would require effective leadership and organization to achieve, and that seems to be something they're not really geared to aim for (any more than Anarchs are.)</div> </div> </div> </div>They're not intrinsically against it, and the modern world makes it ever easier to organize around ideas and goals. Survivor is a pretty natural goal, and it would make sense for them to start coordinating some things and sharing information to achieve it. They also have less to loose when taking bold actions, like breaching the Masquerade.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}